Description:
GenoSafe is a CRO providing analytical testing services for the evaluation of quality, safety and efficacy of Gene and Cell therapy candidates including :
   - GLP biodistribution, shedding and immunogenicity studies ;
   - QC testing, such as viral titration, safety and potency/efficacy testing ;
   - GCP bioanalysis of patient samples, including immunogenicity, shedding and gene expression studies.

GenoSafe brings more than 15 years of experience in the development, qualification and validation of key analytical methods for product and sample testing.

X Santé Biotech a pour but de favoriser la participation de la communauté X dans le secteur de la santé : biotechnologies, medtech, IA santé et e-santé, en :
• créant un réseau amical et informel d’échanges et de réflexions ;
• sensibilisant l’ensemble de la communauté des anciens élèves de l’Ecole polytechnique (les « X ») aux problématiques liées à la santé ;
• créant un réseau professionnel d’X et non-X impliqués dans la santé, en France et à l’étranger, en particulier dans pour favoriser le développement de l’industrie de la santé en France et en Europe ; 
• attirant plus d’étudiants X vers le secteur de la santé ;
• établissant une coopération efficace avec le Corps Enseignant.

Le groupe X Santé Biotech s’intéresse à l’ensemble des activités liées aux Sciences de la Vie, et notamment aux enjeux scientifiques, éthiques et industriels des avancées majeures dans ces domaines.

Since its creation in 1977, the overarching objective of the B3OA was to develop innovative strategies for the diagnosis, surgical treatment, and rehabilitation of patients with orthopaedic-related disorders (resulting from trauma or degenerative disease). 
Specifically, the B3OA’s research focuses on:
- reinforcing current knowledge of pathophysiological and fundamental aspects of osteo-articular repair;
- elaborating innovative biotherapies for enhancing osteo-articular repair ;
- developing new procedures in clinical research for osteo-articular diseases.
Its expert knowledge and skills in tissue engineering, imaging, and cellular and molecular biology allow the laboratory to develop new and innovative translational approaches in orthopedic, odontology, and radiology medical fields.

Based in Marseille, France, World Bio Consulting (WBC) provides scientific advice and support services to projects in the field of biomedical research, fundamental research, preclinical and clinical, therapeutic and diagnostic areas.

WBC provides a full range of services to Biotech, Med-tech or Pharma companies or other related organizations and aims to help start-ups reach their full potential.

Services include:
- The evaluation and validation of a technology, a product, a patent or a project;
- The structuring and implementation of the different stages of Research and Development;
- Planning and strategic implementation;
- Support during the scientific phases, validation, testing, presentation and patent preparation, negotiation and implementation of marketing strategy and internationalization; 
- Reviews of scientific and commercial opportunities;
- The development of the startup’s activities and structure to allow a good positioning on the international market.

WBC helps its customers, with an international network of experts and partners in the health, e-health and life sciences fields, by providing them support and solutions that maximize their potential development and minimize delays.

@AIS Biotech (with AIS for Anti Infective Sugar) is a French Biotech company based in the @Région Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes, France, incorporated in March 2023 with the objective of developing a new class of sugar-based anti-infective biotherapeutics to fight (re)emerging infectious diseases.
Thanks to a Bioengineering plateform based on the expertise of the leading edge academic laboratory @CERMAV (@CNRS, @UGA, Grenoble, France), AIS Biotech aims to develop a pipeline of innovative sugar-based biopharmaceuticals which can prevent or treat infections by mimicking the natural host surface oligosaccharide binding-sites of pathogens. 
GlycoFlu, our first drug-candidate validated at the preclinical stage by the #VirPath laboratory (@CIRI, @INSERM, @cnrs, @UCBL1, @ENS Lyon) and its Technology Research Platform @VirNext (@ucbl1), is developed to prevent or treat infections by human Influenza viruses, a global public health concern with a large socio-economic impact.

